              <div class="related-faq"><span>Related questions</span><a href="/common-concerns#causes">What causes foundation problems?</a><a href="/common-concerns#watering">Will watering my foundation help?</a></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="answerPanel_monitor" class="answer-panel" style="display:none">
          <div class="answer-card">
            <h2 class="card-question">When is "monitor and wait" the right answer?</h2>
            <div class="card-answer">
              <p>When movement is cosmetic, stable, or seasonal. Not every crack needs repair. Monitoring is a legitimate recommendation — we recommend it when it's the honest answer.</p>
              <div class="nm-note">NM context: Seasonal cycling means some movement is normal and does not progress.</div>
              <div class="industry-note">No sales‑only company can recommend monitoring — it generates no revenue. TLS can, and does. We've told homeowners to wait. We'll tell you too, if that's the honest answer.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-links">
              <div class="primary-links">
              </div>
              <div class="related-terms"><span>Related terms</span><a href="/glossary#cosmetic-crack">Cosmetic crack</a><a href="/glossary#active-movement">Active movement</a><a href="/glossary#seasonal-movement">Seasonal movement</a></div>
              <div class="related-faq"><span>Related questions</span><a href="/common-concerns#wait">Will problems get worse if I wait?</a><a href="/common-concerns#wait">Is this serious?</a></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="answerPanel_wrong-repair" class="answer-panel" style="display:none">
          <div class="answer-card">
            <h2 class="card-question">What happens if the wrong repair method is used?</h2>
            <div class="card-answer">
              <p>Installing settlement piers on a heaving foundation makes it worse. Misdiagnosis is real. Investigation before repair is the only protection.</p>
              <div class="nm-note">NM context: Heave is common but symptoms look like settlement. Getting the wrong repair is expensive.</div>
              <div class="industry-note">This is the risk the industry never discusses. A misdiagnosed foundation — heave treated as settlement — can be actively damaged by the repair. Investigation is not optional.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-links">
              <div class="primary-links">
                <a href="/expansive-soil" class="card-link">Expansive Soils →</a>
              </div>
