              <div class="related-faq"><span>Related questions</span><a href="/common-concerns#heave">What's the difference between settlement and heave?</a><a href="/common-concerns#choose">How do I choose a company?</a></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="answerPanel_methods" class="answer-panel" style="display:none">
          <div class="answer-card">
            <h2 class="card-question">What are the different foundation repair methods?</h2>
            <div class="card-answer">
              <p>Helical piers, push piers, drainage correction, poly foam, carbon fiber, etc. The method follows the investigation. No method is selected before we know the soil.</p>
              <div class="nm-note">NM context: Helical piers are appropriate where piers are warranted. Push piers often don't work for residential weight in NM soils.</div>
              <div class="industry-note">Every company promotes the method they sell. The honest answer: the method follows the investigation. If someone is selling you a method before they've seen your soil, they're selling a product, not a solution.</div>
            </div>
